    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is derived purely from the owner's own fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), so I added it as a computed response field rather than a stored/pipeline-assigned one \u2014 this way both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` expose it through their shared mapper.\n\nThree small, cohesive edits:\n\n1. **New `MembershipNumber` helper** (`rest/function/owner/MembershipNumber.java`) \u2014 a fresh single-method class (mirroring the existing `HouseholdId.of` / `Namesakes.countBefore` pattern) that formats `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, `YY` being `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` zero-padded. Returns `null` when either input is absent, so seed/list owners without a code or date don't NPE. Zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **One `@Mapping` line** in `OwnerMapper` delegating `membershipNumber` to that helper \u2014 no existing method's body grew.\n\n3. **One property** added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nStructural impact is minimal: no existing method body was enlarged, the only edited method (`toOwnerDto`) has CC 1 and sits in an interface with no method bodies, and all new logic lives in an isolated class with `WMC_other = 0`.",
